Alle Vælg kontinenter × Luk Vælg kontinenter Vælg region Alle Fjernjob × Luk Inkluder fjernjob Kun on-site job Kun fjernjob Inkluder fjernjob Vælg stillinger × Luk Alle Vælg frekvens × Luk Daglig Hver tredje dag En gang om ugen Daglig Sprog × Luk Engelsk Svensk Norsk Dansk Finsk Tysk Fransk Hollandsk Italiensk Spansk Engelsk, Svensk, Norsk, Dansk Gem jobnotifikation BI Norwegian Business School BI is an independent, not-for-profit foundation and the main provider of research based knowledge on business and management disciplines in Norway. Se ledige stillinger Abonner på nye stillinger Besøg website Adskillige steder Oslo, Norge Bergen, Norge Stavanger, Norge Trondheim, Norge Top 50 European Business School Financial Times rankings 2025 20092 Students 119 Nationalities 30% Of faculty is international BI is a Triple Crown school Schools that achieve all three accreditations, the European EQUIS (European\n                                Quality\n                                Improvement Systems), the American AACSB (The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools\n                                of Business) and the British AMBA (The Association of MBAs), are called Triple Crown\n                                Schools. Less than 1 % of business schools worldwide have achieved triple accreditation.\n                                The accreditations are proof of BI's rigorous standards. Our strategic foundation At BI Norwegian Business School, we are dedicated to delivering education and research\n                                that truly makes a difference. With a rich history spanning over eight decades, BI has\n                                already left an enduring mark on countless individuals, improved business practices, and\n                                shaped our society for the better. However, we operate in an ever-changing landscape characterised by increased competition,\n                                rapid technological advancements, shifting financial frameworks and changing student\n                                preferences. Our Strategy 2030 sets clear goals for how we aim to secure and further develop our\n                                    position as a world-class international business school, recognised by its Triple\n                                    Crown accreditation. BI remains committed to what we regard as our most important societal contribution, which\n                                is to offer a broad access to education, empowering individuals irrespective of their\n                                backgrounds to transform their lives and careers. At BI, we say that “we don't care where you are coming from, only where you're\n                                    going”. Our mission Our research and education contribute to solving society's greatest\n                                        challenges. We give businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the\n                                        opportunity\n                                        to build meaningful careers. Our vision The business school for innovative knowledge and learning -\n                                        transforming\n                                        lives, businesses and society. Research and teaching We will prioritise high-quality research that improves business\n                                practices, solves\n                                societal challenges, and contributes to the global knowledge base. Our researchers and\n                                their work will provide visible, actionable insights that are societally valuable. Research excellence Develop flagship research centres that achieve excellence\n                                through top\n                                publications and secure self-funding through competitive external grants. Establish and promote interdisciplinary research centres that partner with\n                                businesses to drive innovation and real-world application. Relevance and impact Enhance visibility and recognition of BI's research through\n                                intensified engagement in the public debate, media outlets, research communication and\n                                practice-oriented channels. Strengthen collaboration with business, alumni and\n                                    policy-makers, reinforcing the practical relevance of our research. Funding Increase EU and national research grants to strengthen\n                                research capacity. Boost external funding from businesses, foundations, organisations\n                                    and individuals while upholding academic integrity and independence. Nina Vogt Nina is a lecturer at the Department of Marketing. Find out about\n                            her “out of\n                            the box” teaching style. Giovanni Pagliardi Giovanni is a lecturer at the Department of Finance. Find out about\n                            his methods to inspire his students. Mark Brown Mark is an Associate Professor at the Department of Communication\n                            and Culture. Find out how he prepares his students for success. Why work in Norway? Norwegians don't like to brag, but we'll give it a shot: We're a country\n                            known for our beautiful nature, focus on work-life balance, world-leading gender equality\n                            and high rankings in the World Happiness Report. A safe, happy, and stable society Norway scores high in human development, quality of life, and is among the safest\n                                    places in the world. The Scandinavian Leadership Model Norway ranks second in the world in productivity, despite having short working weeks\n                                    and a flat hierarchy leadership model. Sustainability is made a priority Norway is in the middle of a major transition, preparing for an oil-free future,\n                                    which makes this country an exciting place to be. Mind-blowing nature and city life Experience urban cities surrounded by mountains, woods and oceans, and travel beyond\n                                    to explore uninhibited terrain. A diverse and inclusive environment Norway is one of the most gender equal countries in the world, with strong measures\n                                    to ensure equality in the workplace. Healthy work-life balance Employers recognise the importance of having a life outside the office, and a\n                                    collective understanding that family and health come first. Join us! Continual skills development is our driving force, a dynamic and\n                                flexible working environment our reward. At BI we have exciting challenges in a\n                                stimulating international milieu. With over 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000\n                                alumni, BI Norwegian Business School is considered one of the largest and most\n                                influential business schools in Europe. BI offers a varied and comprehensive portfolio of Bachelor's, Master's, PhD and Executive\n                                education programmes and courses. Our partnerships and collaborations with leading\n                                Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions, contribute to\n                                raising the quality of our educational offer. BI's Strategy 2030 has defined clear goals to ensure that the school delivers knowledge\n                                that makes a difference through first-class research and unique learning experiences. We\n                                give businesses the knowledge they need to succeed and people the opportunity to build\n                                meaningful careers. Jobs from this employer Viser job 