      "description": "BI Norwegian Business School - Academic Positions Regio Sitetaal Talen voor vacatures Kies je regio Selecteer de regio die het beste past bij je locatie of voorkeuren. International Sverige Norge Danmark Suomi United Kingdom Deutschland France België Nederland Österreich Schweiz Italia España Volgende Kies je sitetaal Deze instelling regelt de taal van de gebruikersinterface, inclusief knoppen, menu's en alle tekst op de site. Selecteer je voorkeurstaal voor de beste browse-ervaring. Engels English Zweeds Svenska Noors Norsk Deens Dansk Fins Suomi Duits Deutsch Frans Français Nederlands Nederlands Italiaans Italiano Spaans Español Volgende Kies de talen voor vacatures Selecteer de talen voor vacatures die je wilt zien. Deze instelling bepaalt welke vacatures aan jou worden getoond. Engels English Zweeds Svenska Noors Norsk Deens Dansk Fins Suomi Duits Deutsch Frans Français Nederlands Nederlands Italiaans Italiano Spaans Español Instellingen opslaan Job Match Comparison Compare your profile with the job requirements Job or profile information is not available. Why this job matches your profile We've compared your profile to the job requirements. Here's where they align. Job or profile information is not available. Vacatures zoeken Werkgevers zoeken Loopbaanadvies Voor werkgevers Inloggen Vacatures zoeken Werkgevers zoeken Loopbaanadvies Voor werkgevers Inloggen × You have already applied for this position.\n    For questions regarding your application, please contact the employer.\n    For technical assistance, reach out to our support team here . × You have already applied for this position. You can instead create a job alert . × Thank you for your application! An email confirmation has been sent to your email. Loading job alert... × Ontvang vacaturemeldingen die passen bij jouw voorkeuren. Zoekopdracht Select employers Search and select specific employers to receive job alerts only from them. Kies een of meer vakgebieden × Sluiten Alle Kies een of meer deelgebieden Alle Kies een of meer continenten × Sluiten Kies een of meer continenten Kies een of meer regio's Alle Banen op afstand × Sluiten Banen op afstand opnemen Alleen banen op locatie Alleen banen op afstand Banen op afstand opnemen Kies een of meer functies × Sluiten Alle Kies een frequentie × Sluiten Dagelijks Om de drie dagen Eén keer per week Dagelijks Kies een of meer talen × Sluiten Engels Zweeds Noors Deens Fins Duits Frans Nederlands Italiaans Spaans Engels, Nederlands E-mailalert opslaan BI Norwegian Business School BI is an independent, not-for-profit foundation and the main provider of research based knowledge on business and management disciplines in Norway. Vacatures bekijken Maak een e-mailalert aan Website bezoeken Diverse locaties Oslo, Noorwegen Bergen, Noorwegen Stavanger, Noorwegen Trondheim, Noorwegen Top 50 European Business School Financial Times rankings 2025 20092 Students 119 Nationalities 30% Of faculty is international BI is a Triple Crown school Schools that achieve all three accreditations, the European EQUIS (European\n                                Quality\n                                Improvement Systems), the American AACSB (The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools\n                                of Business) and the British AMBA (The Association of MBAs), are called Triple Crown\n                                Schools. Less than 1 % of business schools worldwide have achieved triple accreditation.\n                                The accreditations are proof of BI's rigorous standards. Our strategic foundation At BI Norwegian Business School, we are dedicated to delivering education and research\n                                that truly makes a difference. With a rich history spanning over eight decades, BI has\n                                already left an enduring mark on countless individuals, improved business practices, and\n                                shaped our society for the better. However, we operate in an ever-changing landscape characterised by increased competition,\n                                rapid technological advancements, shifting financial frameworks and changing student\n                                preferences. Our Strategy 2030 sets clear goals for how we aim to secure and further develop our\n                                    position as a world-class international business school, recognised by its Triple\n                                    Crown accreditation. BI remains committed to what we regard as our most important societal contribution, which\n                                is to offer a broad access to education, empowering individuals irrespective of their\n                                backgrounds to transform their lives and careers. At BI, we say that “we don't care where you are coming from, only where you're\n                                    going”. Our mission Our research and education contribute to solving society's greatest\n                                        challenges. We give businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the\n                                        opportunity\n                                        to build meaningful careers. Our vision The business school for innovative knowledge and learning -\n                                        transforming\n                                        lives, businesses and society. Research and teaching We will prioritise high-quality research that improves business\n                                practices, solves\n                                societal challenges, and contributes to the global knowledge base. Our researchers and\n                                their work will provide visible, actionable insights that are societally valuable. Research excellence Develop flagship research centres that achieve excellence\n                                through top\n                                publications and secure self-funding through competitive external grants. Establish and promote interdisciplinary research centres that partner with\n                                businesses to drive innovation and real-world application. Relevance and impact Enhance visibility and recognition of BI's research through\n                                intensified engagement in the public debate, media outlets, research communication and\n                                practice-oriented channels. Strengthen collaboration with business, alumni and\n                                    policy-makers, reinforcing the practical relevance of our research. Funding Increase EU and national research grants to strengthen\n                                research capacity. Boost external funding from businesses, foundations, organisations\n                                    and individuals while upholding academic integrity and independence. Nina Vogt Nina is a lecturer at the Department of Marketing. Find out about\n                            her “out of\n                            the box” teaching style. Giovanni Pagliardi Giovanni is a lecturer at the Department of Finance. Find out about\n                            his methods to inspire his students. Mark Brown Mark is an Associate Professor at the Department of Communication\n                            and Culture. Find out how he prepares his students for success. Why work in Norway? Norwegians don't like to brag, but we'll give it a shot: We're a country\n                            known for our beautiful nature, focus on work-life balance, world-leading gender equality\n                            and high rankings in the World Happiness Report. A safe, happy, and stable society Norway scores high in human development, quality of life, and is among the safest\n                                    places in the world. The Scandinavian Leadership Model Norway ranks second in the world in productivity, despite having short working weeks\n                                    and a flat hierarchy leadership model. Sustainability is made a priority Norway is in the middle of a major transition, preparing for an oil-free future,\n                                    which makes this country an exciting place to be. Mind-blowing nature and city life Experience urban cities surrounded by mountains, woods and oceans, and travel beyond\n                                    to explore uninhibited terrain. A diverse and inclusive environment Norway is one of the most gender equal countries in the world, with strong measures\n                                    to ensure equality in the workplace. Healthy work-life balance Employers recognise the importance of having a life outside the office, and a\n                                    collective understanding that family and health come first. Join us! Continual skills development is our driving force, a dynamic and\n                                flexible working environment our reward. At BI we have exciting challenges in a\n                                stimulating international milieu. With over 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000\n                                alumni, BI Norwegian Business School is considered one of the largest and most\n                                influential business schools in Europe. BI offers a varied and comprehensive portfolio of Bachelor's, Master's, PhD and Executive\n                                education programmes and courses. Our partnerships and collaborations with leading\n                                Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions, contribute to\n                                raising the quality of our educational offer. BI's Strategy 2030 has defined clear goals to ensure that the school delivers knowledge\n                                that makes a difference through first-class research and unique learning experiences. We\n                                give businesses the knowledge they need to succeed and people the opportunity to build\n                                meaningful careers. Jobs from this employer Vacatures weergeven in Engels, Nederlands Instellingen wijzigen BI Norwegian Business School Oslo, Noorwegen Assistant Professor 2 tenure-track roles in Strategy & Entrepreneurship (Oslo): PhD, strong publication pipeline, high-quality teaching. Bonus: digital business, platforms, AI, analytics. 1 dag geleden geplaatst Sluit op: 2026-09-30 (Europe/Oslo) Universitair (hoofd)docent BI Norwegian Business School Oslo, Noorwegen PhD Candidate 4-year funded PhD on human-centered data governance, privacy & smart environments; focus on user/communication aspects. Based in Oslo with 25% teaching and international collaboration. 3 weken geleden geplaatst Sluit over 4 dag(en) PhD Locatie werkgever Nydalsveien 37, 0484 Oslo Noorwegen Kong Christian Frederiks Plass 5, 5006 Bergen Noorwegen Byfjordparken 17, 4007 Stavanger Noorwegen Brattorkaia 16, 7010 Trondheim Noorwegen Vacatures per vakgebied Machinaal Leren 267 Kunstmatige intelligentie 243 Elektrotechniek 169 Materiaalkunde 160 Computationele wetenschappen 122 Moleculaire biologie 114 Electronica 109 Chemische techniek 108 Bioinformatica 107 Programmeertalen 99 Vacatures per functietype PhD 394 Postdoc 346 Universitair (hoofd)docent 148 Hoogleraar 132 Onderzoeker 97 Onderzoekstechnicus 81 Docent / Lector 77 Tenure Track 66 Onderzoeksassistent 57 Management / Leiderschap 54 Vacatures per land België 190 Zweden 151 Finland 126 Marokko 118 Zwitserland 110 Duitsland 107 Nederland 98 Luxemburg 95 Oostenrijk 72 Frankrijk 35 Vacatures per werkgever Mohammed VI Polytechnic Unive... 118 KU Leuven 91 University of Luxembourg 91 ETH Zürich 61 KTH Royal Institute of Techno... 58 University of Turku 47 Eindhoven University of Techn... 42 University of Cologne 41 Karolinska Institutet 39 imec 35 Meer categorieën bekijken Zet de volgende stap in je academische carrière Voor werkzoekenden Vacatures zoeken Werkgevers zoeken Over ons Inloggen Maak een e-mailalert aan Neem contact met ons op Vacatures zoeken PhD Postdoc Onderzoeker Docent/sr. docent Universitair (hoofd)docent Hoogleraar Tenuretrack Ingenieur Onderzoeksassistent Management Voor werkgevers Vacatures Abonnementen Employer branding Succesverhalen Advies voor werkgevers © Academic Media Group International AB. All rights reserved Juridisch | Wij maken gebruik van cookies"
